# Tools

Every tool exports a **`registerX(server: McpServer)`** function that calls `server.registerTool(...)`.
Registration is centralized in `src/tools/index.ts` via `registerAllTools`.

## Entity folders

Place tools under CRM entity folders (not agent modules). Path: `src/tools/<entity>/<tool-kebab>.ts`.

Canonical folders:

- `auth/` — password/auth flows (`AuthService`)
- `costumers/` — customer lookups (`CostumerService`; historical spelling)
- `leads/` — lead/prospect operations
- `memberships/` — memberships and membership discounts
- `categories/` — discount categories
- `allied-commerces/` — allied commerce lookups
- `support-logs/` — support/sales case logs

**One `registerTool` per file** — do not put distinct operations in the same `.ts`. Choose the folder by the primary service/entity the tool calls.

## Definition (Zod + annotations)

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod'
import type { McpServer } from '@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/mcp.js'
import { ok, mapApiError } from '@tools/tool-result.js'

export function registerGetExample(server: McpServer): void {
  server.registerTool(
    'get_example',
    {
      title: 'Obtener ejemplo',
      description: 'When to use, what it returns, and which IDs come from which other tools.',
      inputSchema: {
        id: z.number().int().positive().describe('Entity id. Ejemplo: 12'),
        limit: z.number().int().positive().optional().describe('Máximo de items (opcional)'),
      },
      outputSchema: {
        items: z.array(z.unknown()),
        total: z.number(),
      },
      annotations: {
        readOnlyHint: true,
        idempotentHint: true,
        openWorldHint: true,
      },
    },
    async ({ id, limit }) => {
      const service = new ExampleService()
      const result = await service.getById(id)
      if (!result.success || !result.data) {
        return mapApiError(result.error, 'No se pudo obtener el ejemplo')
      }
      return ok({ items: [result.data], total: 1 }, `Ejemplo #${id} obtenido`)
    },
  )
}
```

## Registration (`src/tools/index.ts`)

1. Export `registerX` from the tool file
2. Add `registerX` to the `toolRegistrars` array in `registerAllTools`

## Rules

- `name` in snake_case, unique and semantic; always set `title`
- Rich `description` — drives agent tool selection; document tool chaining
- Use Zod `inputSchema` / `outputSchema` (not raw JSON Schema)
- Return `ok(structured, shortSummary)` — never dump full JSON into `content`
- Use `fail` / `mapApiError` for stable error codes (`NOT_FOUND`, `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `UPSTREAM_ERROR`, `RATE_LIMITED`)
- Set annotations: `readOnlyHint` / `destructiveHint` / `idempotentHint` / `openWorldHint`
- Always check `result.success` before returning data
- Prefer researching the CRM endpoint first (`crm-endpoint-research` / `crm-api-researcher`) then implement via `mcp-tool-creator`
